parts.body:
Under § 3216(g), an insurer may **not refuse to renew** an individual hospital, surgical or medical expense policy (or one where at least a third of the premium is for those benefits, but not accident-only coverage) except for listed reasons:

- nonpayment of premiums;
- fraud or intentional misrepresentation of material fact;
- discontinuing a class of policies (with **90 days'** notice and an offer of other coverage);
- leaving the individual market entirely (with **180 days'** notice);
- moving out of a network plan's service area; or
- other reasons allowed by the superintendent under HIPAA.

**In no event** may the insurer refuse renewal because of anyone's physical or mental condition or health, or require a limiting rider as a condition of renewal.
